mustuse_abandoned.vyrn:20:0: `ops` may not be dropped: it is a second name for the `read` parameter `self`
  fix: `consume` the place where `ops` is bound, so `ops` takes the value rather than naming it
  fix: delete the `drop`: the place that owns it releases it
mustuse_abandoned.vyrn:35:9: `a` is a `Txn` and is never disposed
  note: `Txn` declares `impl MustUse`, so a value of it must be handed on by name on every path: passed to a `consume` parameter, forwarded by returning it, or released with `drop a`
mustuse_abandoned.vyrn:38:9: `b` is a `Txn` and is disposed more than once
  note: `Txn` declares `impl MustUse`, so a value of it must be handed on by name on every path: passed to a `consume` parameter, forwarded by returning it, or released with `drop b`
mustuse_abandoned.vyrn:42:9: `c` is a `Txn` and is never disposed
  note: `Txn` declares `impl MustUse`, so a value of it must be handed on by name on every path: passed to a `consume` parameter, forwarded by returning it, or released with `drop c`
mustuse_abandoned.vyrn:47:13: `pool` is an `Array<Txn>` and is never disposed
  note: `Txn` declares `impl MustUse` and a `Array<Txn>` holds one, so the `Array<Txn>` must be handed on by name on every path: passed to a `consume` parameter, forwarded by returning it, or released with `drop pool`, which releases what it holds
